WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.960
once, there was an abomination

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.000
who had no place in this world

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.080
a dragon crossbreed, feared by the gods

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.780
and described as an antithesis to all life

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.760
clutching a strange doll and truly alone

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:22.560
eventually this pale, white haired girl was drawn into a cold and lonely painted world

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.420
and much later, perhaps within many layers of these painted worlds

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:32.560
a scaled, snake eyed young girl becomes the last hope for humanity

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.600
we've talked at length already about the paintings

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.520
but it bears repeating, basically

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.860
they're self contained universes that

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:44.860
exist within themselves and from what we can gather

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:49.500
the original in the overworld is the Painted World of Ariamis in Anor Londo

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.360
which is protected by the Painting Guardians

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:58.180
and, as any painting does, really, these painting reflect the themes of the outside world

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:02.780
with the cycle of death and rebirth, just like our world

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:08.480
so, inevitably, just like the flame will fade, a painting will become rotten

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:13.320
and when this happens, the residents make the decision to set their world aflame

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:18.340
then, escaping into yet another painted world, as their world burns behind them

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.340
so that they can live on

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.600
"Ashen One, I cannot die"

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.600
"I have a world to paint"

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:33.300
this painter has no name, so we've taken to calling her Aria

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.700
and, to paint a new world, she must see flame

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.460
"Those who aren't kin to fire"

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.900
"Cannot paint a world"

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.560
"Those absorbed by fire"

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.800
"Must not paint a world"

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.880
"Don't worry"

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.280
"I haven't forgotten, Mother"

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:56.140
so just as her mother was once shown flame,

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.060
Aria, too, must have an awareness of it

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.720
so, in our fight with another unkindled, Friede,

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:06.440
the friction of our clash sets the world aflame

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.360
yet, Aria is left wanting for one more thing

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.340
"Ashen One, thy gift of flame has taken route"

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:18.160
"And Uncle Gael will soon bring the pigment"

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.060
"Pigment..."

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:23.140
"Colored like the dark soul of man"

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:28.420
since the dark soul of man has never been retreived from the Ringed City,

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:32.920
it follows that a painting with this dark soul as the pigment

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.640
will be different than the paintings before it

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:38.280
"I wish to paint a picture"

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:43.540
"Of a cold, dark, and very gentle place"

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.780
"Soon, Uncle Gael will bring me the pigment"

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:49.640
Gael

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:55.040
when we first met Gael in Ariandel, we didn't really think too much of him

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:00.720
he's a soft-spoken, reverent man in undying service to his lady of the painting

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:05.740
and, in many ways, Gael isn't supposed to be much more than just a simple undead

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.760
the core of what being undead really represents

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.760
however, saying that,

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.140
his two item descriptions, back then,

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.380
they revealed an unusually staggering depth to his history

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.420
because Gael has been around for a long time

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.060
he alone recalls the Way of White Corona miracle

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:27.560
which was something that was thought to have been lost to the ages

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.460
for, long ago,

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.300
when the gods still had their imprint left upon the world

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:34.560
in Dark Souls 1

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.700
reciting any of their miracles

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.360
would conjure up these white disks

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:42.240
and, back then, apparently, also

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:44.720
were these slave knights

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:46.960
an order that Gael was a part of

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.520
and Gael's slave knight armor, embellished with this red cloth,

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:53.520
was once a symbol of honor

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:58.580
but in stark contrast to this honor, slave knights had a terrible duty

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:01.680
they were used as fodder in the bleakest of battles

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:06.020
imagine, they were the knights that were sent first to tire out the enemy

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.720
because, after all, they couldn't die

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:14.060
and so, we know that at least one slave knight outlived his masters

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.860
for, while the slave knights were never relieved from duty,

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:21.800
Gael did eventually find refuge in the painted world,

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.300
which leads us to believe that whatever entity they served,

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.380
the slave knights outlived them

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.340
able to go mad, but unable to die

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.080
"My lady lives in the cold land of Ariandel"

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.400
"I need you to show her flame"

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:42.760
"A proper flame that will burn the rot away"

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.120
and so,

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.820
this ancient, old undead found a new purpose

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.920
one that he believed in wholeheartedly

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:54.140
first, to save his painted world from the tyranny of Friede

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.700
and then, to help his lady create a new world

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.080
this one, painted with the dark soul of legend

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:05.420
and, if there's any one positive attribute to take from the dark soul,

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:07.920
it would probably be immortality

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:11.120
and, perhaps this will be a painting that does not rot

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:17.080
but it is impossible to know exactly what kind of world will be painted with the dark soul

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:21.300
but I do have faith in the good of this ending, validated by one thing,

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.760
Gael's character

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:27.280
because, until very end of time, Gael fights for this new world

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:32.240
he weathers countless battles, he even knows that a terrible fate awaits him

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.080
and this is a man that has been around since the Age of Fire

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:40.400
what other character in the series can lay claim to the knowledge that represents

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:45.540
so, given that he has the right to knowledge of the dark soul, more than most characters,

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:50.340
and, given that he actually told Aria to paint this world,

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.080
"I'll head off to paint"

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.640
"I promised Uncle Gael I would"

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:59.180
and, that he expects us to be thankful in the end

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:02.380
"You will thank me when it's done"

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:03.780
you can conclude

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.240
that his quest to find the dark soul is a noble one

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:10.580
"If it is the dark soul thou desirest,"

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:14.340
"Then seek Filianore's church,"

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.180
"At the base of the cliff"

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:19.580
"There wilt thou the sleeping princess waken"

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.260
"Her slumber..."

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:22.960
"Is a deceit "

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.660
"A lid, covering an overgrown privy"

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:31.280
"A prop, to keep thee from the dark soul of thine desire"

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:36.580
upon her awakening, I expect Filianore fully believed that she would see the face

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.740
of her father staring back at her

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:42.140
alas, an unkindled wakes her from her slumber,

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:46.340
and in a flash of light, we are transported to an apocalyptic scene

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:47.960
the end of the world

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:53.460
what exactly happens, though, in this cutscene is very worthy of debate

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.600
some people believe that the entire city was an illusion

00:06:56.620 --> 00:07:00.140
and that Filianore's faith simply kept it in check

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:04.140
somewhat like how Gwyndolin kept the sun shining in Anor Londo

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:09.280
but, another theory is that this flash of light takes us forward in time

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.520
to the very end

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.820
light, after all, is time

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:17.920
personally, though, not only do I believe we are transported forward in time,

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:22.500
I think we are the only one to experience this rapid skip forward

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:23.840
let me explain that

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:25.740
so, everyone else here,

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:30.380
Gael, the pygmy lords, Filianore, Shira,

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:36.100
it's likely they fully experienced every inexorable second of time

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.560
scraping by until this point

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:40.660
where Filianore finally dies

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.500
"Filianore"

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:48.300
"Help me, please"

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.400
"The Red Hood is come to eat us"

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.860
"To eat our dark souls"

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:59.900
the proof that time has passed is in all of these characters

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:00.920
for example,

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:04.080
the pygmy lords knew that Gael was searching for them

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:09.860
they knew long enough that he earned the terrifying mantle of the Red Hood

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.140
the Red Hood is come to eat us

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:15.440
rumors like that don't just appear in one flash of light

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:19.780
also, Gael's weaponry is a testament to time passing

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:21.820
his blade is broken and chipped,

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.540
and his crossbow is stained and twisted

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.160
they weren't like that before

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:29.280
and Gael himself, on some level,

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:33.460
is surprised to see that you still exist in this world

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.300
"What, still here?"

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.240
Shira, however, has been looking for you

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:44.620
"I've searched for thee, dark stricken creature"

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:45.880
"I am Shira"

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:52.760
"Daughter of the duke, descendant of gods, and trusted friend to Midir"

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:54.020
"At once,"

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:59.240
"I am the honor of the gods, the glory of fire, and the fear of the dark"

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.860
"Thou shalt not go unpunished"

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.000
"For thy treachery"

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.000
"Thy profanity"

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.500
"And thy shameless yearning"

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:11.500
She, too, made it to the end of the world

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:14.920
Her soul enduring in the name of her long lost gods.

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:18.220
Treachery, profanity and yearning

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:24.660
So, assumedly, our treachery could be our disloyalty to the gods as humans

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.660
Our profanity could be the dark within us

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:35.240
And our yearning is the want and will of all humans that is described in a lot of dark item descriptions

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:43.720
"Never would I ever forgive thy lowly kind"

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:47.200
Even till the end of time, she never left that dark room

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:54.380
Unaware or uncaring that only a few dunes away the pygmy lords are being devoured alive,

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:55.500
by Gael,

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:59.600
the final antagonist of the Dark Soul series

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:03.720
I see a lot of people complaining that for a final boss

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:09.380
We don't hear a single word about this character until the DLC of Dark Souls III

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.900
But, then, is that really so strange?

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.880
As we mentioned before, Gael is much like us

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:20.520
He is a simple undead, characterized by an uncrushable resolve

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:25.880
"Hand it over that thing, your dark soul"

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:31.620
"For my lady's painting"

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:47.380
The red hooded wandering slave knight Gael sought the blood of the dark soul as pigment for the painted world

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:50.080
But Gael knew that he was no champion

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:55.240
that the dark soul would likely ruin him and he had little hope of a safe return

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:58.060
So why do you think he led you here?

00:10:58.060 --> 00:10:59.340
To kill him, perhaps?

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:04.080
The revelation here is that the soul can exist in the blood

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.720
which is something that shouldn't be too surprising

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:13.520
after all Ariandel flailed himself to satiate the flame within the lord vessel with his blood

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:18.200
Those that feast upon human flesh, some rats in Dark Souls I, for example,

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:21.740
they've always dropped humanity which is a fragment of the soul

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:27.920
and a hollow without blood struggles to be reanimated that we learn this in the cathedral

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:34.660
And the abyss watchers also shared the soul of the Wolfblood master between them

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:40.600
And in much the same way, the blood of the dark soul courses through the pygmy's veins

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:46.360
yet they've existed for so damn long that their blood has long since dried

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:50.360
The painter needs this blood to paint a world

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.100
But how do you paint with dried blood?

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:59.200
Well, one way is to consume it to, digest it and make the blood your own

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:07.200
"Ah"

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.640
"Is this the blood?"

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:17.380
"The blood of the dark soul."

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:48.300
Inflicted by the same frenzy that took Manus,

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:50.680
the same insanity that took Artorias

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:54.960
On some level, Gael is still holding true to his purpose

00:12:55.140 --> 00:13:00.420
Even now, he wonders aloud whether he succeeded in digesting the dark soul

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:06.080
And when he sees us, he doesn't see an old companion, he only sees more blood

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:12.280
Broken great sword in hand, Gael represents more than just a part of the first DLC

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:16.880
Instead, he exists as a true counterpart to the soul of cinder

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:20.900
He is the desire of humanity fighting for a place in the world

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:23.280
He is the frenzy of the dark soul

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:25.420
He is a hollow's loss of self

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:30.540
And he is the souls of countless others that he's consumed in his journey

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.040
Gael died as he lived

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:50.460
As a slave knight, intended for sacrifice

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:54.920
And in the end, whether he guided us here to kill him, or not,

00:13:55.180 --> 00:14:01.700
Gael's final accomplishment was consuming the dark soul, digesting it and bleeding it out

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.820
making the dark soul as whole as it's ever been since the very dawn of time

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:13.240
"My thanks, Ashen one"

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:16.880
"With this, will I paint a world"

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:18.880
"Please tell me thy name"

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:22.020
"I would name this painting after thee"

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.600
"I see"

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:29.040
"We are much alike"

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:32.860
"Then I will name this painting - Ash"

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:39.720
"It will be a cold, dark, and very gentle place"

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:44.740
And one day, it will make someone a goodly home.

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:50.220
I wonder when Uncle Gael intends his return

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:56.060
I hope the new painting will be to him a gentle home

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:03.120
And so,  a little universe is painted within a dying world

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:07.980
A cold, dark and gentle place like the paintings before it

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:14.180
Except this new world has the ineffable dark soul painted into its very fabric

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:17.720
And even when the outside world expires

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:24.440
Whether fire fades, whether it's usurped by a lord of hollows or an accursed undead

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:27.920
Somewhere within the painted world of Ariamis,

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:31.100
hidden within the painted world of Ariandel,

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:36.880
tucked away in a small attic, surrounded by a burning world

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:40.640
is a new sanctuary named Ash

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:46.260
Maybe one day we'll see what this cold, dark, gentle world is like

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:50.600
Miyazaki hasn't completely ruled out Dark Souls IV

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:53.220
So I do feel like it will be made oneday

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.640
But for now and for the foreseeable future, really,

00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:01.580
as you should have expected from the Dark Souls, the ending you envision

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.580
in this new world is all your own

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:07.500
Built upon the excellence of your imagination

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.760
I know you still have questions, so do I

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:15.100
Soon, we'll talk about the layers of time in the Ringed City

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:18.920
The differece between dark sigils and the dark sign

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:24.340
And the statues of primordial serpents and the stories of the locusts

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:26.760
This may be the end for now

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:32.160
"But one day, tiny flames will dance across the darkness"

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:34.660
I'll see you then.

